# messages/{ja,en}.json are emitted by scripts/generate-messages.mjs (predev,
# pretest, prebuild) as JSON.stringify(merged, null, 2). Prettier collapses a
# short array onto one line where JSON.stringify always expands it, so the two
# disagree on `dayLabels` and `prettier --check` can never pass on the committed
# output. That made an unfixable verification step: task 1105 (2026-09-26) ran
# `prettier --check` on these files, honestly recorded "未検証", had the row read
# as a failure, and burned its cost budget repeating the round. Any agent that
# "fixed" it with `prettier --write` instead put unrelated reformatted keys in
# its diff and was failed for scope drift (task 1107).
# CI never checked these: its steps are `**/*.ts` (backend) and
# `src/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,css,md}` (frontend), neither of which matches. Ignoring
# them aligns local checks with CI and leaves formatting to the generator.
messages/ja.json
messages/en.json

